Contract change rule
====================

The contract is tools.json (tool names, parameters, result shapes, error
messages the suite matches on), journal.md (event kinds and the journal
schema) and runtime.md (process start).

Any change to a tool name, a parameter (name, type, optionality, allowed
values), a result shape, or a journal event shape bumps `tool_schema` by one
in tools.json, in the same commit, and adds an entry below. A change to
`journal_schema` (the `v` field) also bumps `tool_schema`. Wording changes
that alter no schema and no matched error text do not bump it.

The plugin declares the `tool_schema` it requires; both implementations and
the conformance suite read the value from tools.json. contract/check_contract.py
fails if tool_schema, the tool list or any example drifts.

Log (newest first)
------------------

tool_schema 2  (slice C1 walkthrough, 2026-11-16)  Journal format change, and a
result-shape narrowing: `interrupted` removed from the journal `end` event's
end_kind enum and from the `end_interview` result enum (a crash or server exit
on an active interview writes no `end` event; `interrupted` is a decision-log
kind only). End-kind triggers stated in journal.md. Added without schema change:
`log_item` duplicate caller-supplied id error row, and the rule that `status`
`items` counts equal the counts derived from `tree` (checked in check_contract.py).
Bumped because the CHANGES rule counts a journal event shape change.

tool_schema 1  (slice C1, 2026-11-16)  Initial freeze: REQ-40 tool list,
journal_schema 2.
